To float a container to the left using SUSY and Sass, you can use margin-left instead of float. [1] For example:

.container {
  @include container;
  margin-left: 1em; // Adjust as needed for offset
}

This will center the container by default, then adjusting the margin-left value moves it to the desired position without disrupting the grid layout.

To solve your issue, you can use absolute positioning for both the background div and content divs within it. This way, only the background image fades out while keeping other elements visible:

```html
<div id="hpbg-image">
    <div id="stuff">
        <div id="header">...</div>
        <div id="search-area">...</div>
        <div id="content1" style="height:150px">No minimum contract, pay for everything online</div>
